  "id": "DrugBank_DB13873 - MONDO_7759",
  "verbalization": "Fenofibric Acid is strongly associated with the condition Hyperlipidemia, Familial Combined, Lpl Related, through a chain of indications that link it to Obsolete Familial Combined Hyperlipidemia. This pathway suggests that Fenofibric Acid may exert its effects by targeting lipid metabolism, as evidenced by its relationship with Ciprofibrate and Fenofibrate, both of which are known to influence lipid profiles. The indirect connection to Ezetimibe, another lipid-lowering agent, further supports the notion that Fenofibric Acid may act through a shared mechanism in modulating lipid metabolism. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a potential role in the regulation of lipoprotein lipase activity, which is central to the pathogenesis of familial combined hyperlipidemia. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Fenofibric Acid contributes to the management of hyperlipidemia, though the exact molecular pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
